.TH KALEIDUX-DAEMON 1 "OCTOBER 2026" "0.0.1-kneecap" "Kaleidux Manual"
.SH NAME
kaleidux-daemon \- High-performance hardware-accelerated wallpaper daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kaleidux-daemon
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kaleidux-daemon
displays images and looping videos on Wayland and X11, with transitions and hardware decoding when available. Video playback uses FFmpeg, libmpv, or GStreamer appsink.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-video-backend \fI<BACKEND>\fR
Select auto, ffmpeg, mpv, or appsink. Auto tries FFmpeg, then mpv, then appsink. An explicitly selected backend reports failures instead of switching backends.
.TP
.B \-\-video-mode \fI<MODE>\fR
Select auto, cpu, cuda, dmabuf, nv12, or rgba. CPU mode disables hardware decoding in FFmpeg and appsink. Other explicit modes require appsink; explicit modes cannot be combined with mpv.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start the daemon in demo mode, cycling through built-in transitions and sample content.
.TP
.B \-\-log \fI<LOG>\fR
Set diagnostic verbosity from 1 (warnings) through 5 (trace-all). Level 4 includes performance diagnostics and adds monitoring overhead.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.B \-\-streamed
Enable the experimental memory policy with smaller media caches and read-ahead. Source cadence and hardware decoding are preserved.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The global main-monitor option selects the default command output. Its default, auto, chooses the largest active pixel area, then the first name in lexical order. kldctl's \-o all targets every output.
.PP
Set volume from 0 to 100 for audio on any video backend. Zero disables audio decoding.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KLD_NATIVE_HWDECODER
FFmpeg decoder preference: auto, software, vulkan, vaapi, nvdec, or another available platform API. Unavailable hardware falls back to supported candidates and then software.
.TP
.B WGPU_BACKEND
Rendering API selection, such as vulkan or gl. This does not select the video decoder.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kaleidux/config.toml
The main configuration file where monitors, content paths, and transitions are defined.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kaleidux/logs/
Directory containing daemon logs if file logging is enabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kldctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mjoyufull <https://github.com/Mjoyufull/Kaleidux>
